.TH CTI-MAILER 1 "2026-10-12" "cti-agent 1.3" "CTI Fleet Manual"
.SH NAME
cti-mailer \- the fleet's single outbound mail channel, behind the recipient allowlist
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cti-mailer
.BI \-\-html " FILE"
.RB [ \-\-text
.IR FILE ]
.RB [ \-\-subject
.IR TEXT ]
.RB [ \-\-to
.IR LIST ]
.RB [ \-\-cc
.IR LIST ]
.RB [ \-\-attach
.IR FILE ]...
.RI [ common ]
.PP
.B cti-mailer
.B \-\-lane
.I NAME
.BI \-\-html " FILE"
.RB [ \-\-text
.IR FILE ]
.RB [ \-\-to
.IR LIST ]
.RB [ \-\-subject
.IR TEXT ]
.RB [ \-\-attach
.IR FILE ]...
.RI [ common ]
.PP
.B cti-mailer
.B \-\-to\-operator
.BI \-\-message " TEXT"
.RB [ \-\-board\-id
.IR ID ]
.RB [ \-\-subject
.IR TEXT ]
.RI [ common ]
.PP
.B cti-mailer \-\-check
.RB [ \-\-from\-mailbox
.IR ADDRESS ]
.PP
where
.I common
is
.RB [ \-\-from\-mailbox
.IR ADDRESS ]
.RB [ \-\-dry\-run ]
.RB [ \-\-require\-approval ]
.RB [ \-\-approve ]
.RB [ \-\-save\-to\-sent
.IR BOOL ].
.PP
.B sudo cti\-agent cti\-mailer
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B cti-mailer
sends one message through Microsoft Graph
.BR sendMail ,
as the fleet mailbox. It is the Go port of
.IR lanes/mailer.py ,
flag for flag and output for output.
.BR run\-appscan (1)
calls it with
.B \-\-lane was
and
.BR run\-domains (1)
with
.BR "\-\-lane dom" ;
.B run\-digest
and
.B run\-patchtuesday
still call
.I mailer.py
until the switch described in RUNBOOK.md section 11b.
.PP
It never guesses a recipient. Every address on To and Cc must pass a
recipient gate, checked before anything is rendered, and the gate is the same
with
.B \-\-dry\-run
as without, so a dry run that succeeds is a send that would be allowed.
Every address must also look like
.IB local @ domain . tld
with no spaces, which
.B \-\-approve
never overrides.
.SS The default gate (no \-\-lane)
.TP
.B To
.B \-\-to
if given, else
.BR DIGEST_TO .
With
.BR \-\-to\-operator ,
.B FLEET_OPERATOR_EMAIL
instead, and
.B \-\-to
is refused.
No recipients at all is refused: there is no default.
.TP
.B Cc
.B \-\-cc
if given, else
.BR DIGEST_CC ,
plus every address on
.B FLEET_ALLOW_TO
when
.B DIGEST_CC_FROM_ALLOW_TO
is true. Anyone already on To is dropped from Cc. An escalation
.RB ( \-\-to\-operator )
is never copied.
.TP
.B Allowlist
.B FLEET_ALLOW_TO
if set, else
.BR DIGEST_TO ,
plus
.B FLEET_OPERATOR_EMAIL
always, compared case-insensitively. It covers To
.B and
Cc. Any address outside it refuses the send, naming every such address,
unless
.B \-\-approve
is given. An unconfigured install therefore fails closed: the scheduled
digest to
.B DIGEST_TO
works and nothing else does.
.SS Lane sends (\-\-lane NAME)
A lane is a second audience with its own pair of variables, named from
.I NAME
in upper case:
.B \-\-lane was
reads
.B WAS_TO
and
.BR WAS_ALLOW_TO ;
.B \-\-lane dom
reads
.B DOM_TO
and
.BR DOM_ALLOW_TO .
.TP
.B No fallback
.IB LANE _ALLOW_TO
unset or empty refuses the send, and
.B \-\-approve
does not change that. Nothing falls back to
.BR DIGEST_TO ,
.B DIGEST_CC
or
.BR FLEET_ALLOW_TO :
that is how a report reaches an audience nobody chose.
.TP
.B Recipients
.B \-\-to
if given, else
.IB LANE _TO
(unset is refused). There is no Cc on a lane send:
.BR \-\-cc ,
.B DIGEST_CC
and
.B \-\-to\-operator
are ignored.
Every recipient must be on the expanded
.IB LANE _ALLOW_TO
or be
.BR FLEET_OPERATOR_EMAIL ,
or the send is refused unless
.B \-\-approve
is given.
.TP
.B References
.IB LANE _ALLOW_TO
(and only a lane allowlist) may include another variable's value with
.B $NAME
or
.BR ${NAME} ,
for example
.BR WAS_ALLOW_TO=$FLEET_ALLOW_TO,appdev@example.com .
A name is letters, digits and underscores, not starting with a digit.
References nest up to 5 deep; a cycle is refused; an address reached twice is
kept once. A reference to a variable that is not in the environment at all is
refused, naming it, rather than read as empty. A variable that is present but
empty contributes nothing, and if the whole list expands to nothing the send
is refused.
.TP
.B No wildcards
Any token beginning with
.B $
that does not name exactly one variable
.RB ( $ ,
.BR ${} ,
.BR $*_ALLOW_TO ,
.BR ${*} )
is refused. There is no way to say
.IR "every allowlist" .
.TP
.B Cross-check
When every lane recipient is also on
.BR DIGEST_TO ,
a note is logged suggesting the list was copied and not edited. It does not
stop the send.
.SS The message
The body is the
.B \-\-html
file as given, or for
.B \-\-message
a short HTML page with the text (escaped, paragraphs split on blank lines)
and reply instructions naming the
.B [FLEET\~\fIID\fB]
tag and the mailbox the orchestrator reads.
The subject is
.B \-\-subject
or
.BR "CTI Brief\~\fIYYYY\-MM\-DD\fR" ;
in message mode with
.B \-\-board\-id
it is prefixed with
.B [FLEET\~\fIID\fB]
unless already present. Whitespace and newlines are collapsed to single
spaces and the subject is cut to 255 bytes. A subject beginning
.B [Sev5]
is sent with high importance. Every message carries the header
.B X\-CTI\-Agent\-Sent
so the digest and
.BR cti\-mailbox (1)
can recognise the fleet's own mail when it comes back.
.PP
Progress goes to standard error as
.B [mailer]
lines: from, to, subject, size, any skipped attachment, and the HTTP status
and Graph request-id of the send. Standard output carries exactly one JSON
line for the runners to parse:
.TP
After a send
.BR sent\~(true) ,
.BR status ,
.BR request_id ,
.BR subject ,
.BR to ,
.B cc
(always a list) and
.B ts
(UTC).
.TP
After \-\-dry\-run
.BR dry_run\~(true) ,
.BR subject ,
.BR to ,
.BR cc ,
.B mode
.RB ( html
or
.BR message ),
and either
.B html
(the file's absolute path) or
.B body
(the rendered escalation).
.PP
.B \-\-check
prints only standard-error lines.
.SH OPTIONS
Go's flag syntax: each option may also be written with a single dash
.RB ( \-html ),
and a value may follow
.B =
or a space.
Exactly one of
.B \-\-html
and
.B \-\-message
is required for a send.
.TP
.BI \-\-html " FILE"
The rendered digest to send as the HTML body. Must exist.
Default:\~none.
.TP
.BI \-\-message " TEXT"
A short plain-text body for an escalation or alert, wrapped in minimal HTML.
Default:\~none.
.TP
.BI \-\-text " FILE"
A plain-text alternative. Accepted because the runners pass it, and logged as
.IR "recorded but not transmitted" :
Graph sends one body. The file is not read.
Default:\~none.
.TP
.BI \-\-subject " TEXT"
The subject line; see
.IR "The message" .
Default:\~\fBCTI Brief \fIYYYY\-MM\-DD\fR (today, local time).
.TP
.BI \-\-to " LIST"
Comma-separated recipients, replacing
.B DIGEST_TO
(or
.IB LANE _TO
with
.BR \-\-lane ).
They still have to pass the allowlist: with no
.B FLEET_ALLOW_TO
the allowlist is
.BR DIGEST_TO ,
not
.BR \-\-to .
Mutually exclusive with
.BR \-\-to\-operator .
Default:\~none.
.TP
.BI \-\-cc " LIST"
Comma-separated Cc recipients, replacing
.BR DIGEST_CC .
Gated by
.B FLEET_ALLOW_TO
exactly like To. Ignored with
.B \-\-lane
and with
.BR \-\-to\-operator .
Default:\~none.
.TP
.BI \-\-lane " NAME"
Send as the named lane, using only
.IB NAME _TO
and
.IB NAME _ALLOW_TO
(upper-cased); see
.IR "Lane sends" .
Default:\~none (the default gate).
.TP
.B \-\-to\-operator
Send to
.B FLEET_OPERATOR_EMAIL
(refused if it is unset). Pre-approved: telling the operator something is not
an outward-facing send. Never copied. Ignored with
.BR \-\-lane .
Default:\~\fBfalse\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-from\-mailbox " ADDRESS"
The sending mailbox. With
.B \-\-check
it is only the address printed on the last line.
Default:\~\fB$GRAPH_MAILBOX\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-board\-id " ID"
The board line the escalation belongs to, so a reply can be matched back.
Adds the
.B [FLEET\~\fIID\fB]
tag to the subject and the reply instructions. Has no effect with
.BR \-\-html .
Default:\~none.
.TP
.BI \-\-attach " FILE"
Attach a file. Repeatable, once per file. A file that cannot be read, or is
over 3,000,000 bytes, is skipped with a log line and the message is sent
without it: the finding is not withheld for want of its evidence. The limit is
per file; keep the total under about 3\~MB, because Graph rejects larger
inline requests. Sent with type
.B text/markdown
for
.I .md
files and
.B text/plain
for everything else, under the file's base name.
Default:\~none.
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
Resolve and gate the recipients, render the body and subject, read the
attachments, print the result JSON, and send nothing. No Graph call is made.
Default:\~\fBfalse\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-require\-approval
Mark this as an off-cycle send: it is refused unless
.B \-\-approve
is also given. Checked after the recipient gate.
Default:\~\fBfalse\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-approve
The operator has approved this specific send, normally after it was posted
to the board tagged
.BR [APPROVE] .
It permits recipients outside the allowlist (default gate) or outside
.IB LANE _ALLOW_TO
(lane), and satisfies
.BR \-\-require\-approval .
It does not permit a malformed address, an unset or empty lane allowlist, an
unresolvable or wildcard reference, or a send with no recipients.
Default:\~\fBfalse\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-save\-to\-sent " BOOL"
Keep a copy in Sent Items. Only the word
.B true
(any case) keeps a copy; every other value, including
.B 1
and
.BR yes ,
means no copy.
Default:\~\fBtrue\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-check
Verify the configuration and the app registration, and send nothing.
Prints the binary's version (with a warning when its commit differs from
.IR /etc/cti\-agent/version ),
the
.I fleet.env
path, then each required setting as
.B OK
or
.B UNSET
and each optional one as
.B OK
or
.BR none .
If any required setting is unset it stops there. Otherwise it requests a
token and reports the tenant, the app ID and the granted application roles:
.B Mail.Read
or
.B Mail.ReadWrite
(read the mailbox) and
.B Mail.Send
are required and reported
.B OK
or
.BR MISSING ;
.B Mail.ReadWrite
for
.BR cti\-mailbox (1)
is reported
.B absent
without failing; any other granted role is listed as
.BR UNUSED .
Of the lane variables only
.BR WAS_TO ,
.BR WAS_ALLOW_TO ,
.B DOM_TO
and
.B DOM_ALLOW_TO
are listed, and references in them are not expanded.
Default:\~\fBfalse\fR.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
Read from the process environment, after
.I fleet.env
is loaded (existing environment variables win). Graph settings are in
section 1 of
.IR fleet.env ,
recipients in section 4.
.TP
.BR TENANT_ID ", " CLIENT_ID ", " CLIENT_SECRET
The app registration. Required for a send and for
.BR \-\-check ;
not read by
.BR \-\-dry\-run .
.TP
.B GRAPH_MAILBOX
The sending mailbox, unless
.B \-\-from\-mailbox
is given. Required.
.TP
.B FLEET_OPERATOR_EMAIL
The escalation address. Always allowed by every gate. Required by
.BR \-\-check .
.TP
.B DIGEST_TO
Default recipients, and the allowlist when
.B FLEET_ALLOW_TO
is empty.
.TP
.B DIGEST_CC
Default Cc recipients. Gated like To.
.TP
.B DIGEST_CC_FROM_ALLOW_TO
.BR true ,
.BR yes ,
.B 1
or
.B on
(any case): also copy every address on
.BR FLEET_ALLOW_TO .
Anything else is off. The operator is not added unless listed there.
.TP
.B FLEET_ALLOW_TO
The default gate's allowlist, covering To and Cc. Literal addresses only;
.B $NAME
is not expanded here. Empty: falls back to
.BR DIGEST_TO .
.TP
.IB LANE _TO ", " LANE _ALLOW_TO
A lane's recipients and allowlist, for example
.BR WAS_TO / WAS_ALLOW_TO
and
.BR DOM_TO / DOM_ALLOW_TO .
No defaults, no fallback.
.TP
.I NAME
Any variable referenced as
.B $NAME
from a lane allowlist.
.TP
.B CTI_REPLY_MAILBOX
The mailbox named in an escalation's reply instructions.
Default:\~the sending mailbox.
.TP
.BR NVD_API_KEY ", " CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN
Only reported by
.BR \-\-check .
.TP
.BR FLEET_ENV ", " FLEET_HOME
The
.I fleet.env
path:
.B FLEET_ENV
if set, else
.IR $FLEET_HOME/fleet.env ,
else
.IR /var/lib/cti\-agent/fleet.env .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/cti\-agent/fleet.env
Settings, recipients and the client secret;
.B root:ctiagent
0640.
.TP
.I /etc/cti\-agent/version
The install record written by
.BR install\-fedora.sh ;
.B \-\-check
compares its
.B commit=
line with the binary. Absent is not an error.
.TP
.I /opt/cti\-agent/bin/cti\-mailer
The binary.
.I /opt/cti\-agent/lanes/mailer.py
is the Python original it replaces.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The message was accepted by Graph; or
.B \-\-dry\-run
passed every check; or
.B \-\-check
found every required setting and role. Skipped attachments, unused roles and
a missing cleanup role do not change this.
.TP
.B 1
Nothing was sent: a setting is missing, the arguments conflict, the HTML file
does not exist, an address is malformed, a recipient is outside the
allowlist without
.BR \-\-approve ,
a lane allowlist is unset or does not resolve,
.B \-\-require\-approval
was given without
.BR \-\-approve ,
the token request failed, or Graph refused the send. With
.BR \-\-check :
a required setting or role is missing, or no token could be obtained.
.TP
.B 2
Unknown option or bad value (Go's flag package).
.SH EXAMPLES
Check configuration and Graph roles:
.PP
.EX
sudo cti\-agent cti\-mailer \-\-check
.EE
.PP
Preview today's digest send without sending:
.PP
.EX
sudo cti\-agent cti\-mailer \e
  \-\-html /var/lib/cti\-agent/reports/digest\-daily\-$(date +%F).html \e
  \-\-subject "CTI Brief $(date +%F)" \-\-dry\-run
.EE
.PP
Preview the weekly domains report to its own audience:
.PP
.EX
sudo cti\-agent cti\-mailer \-\-lane dom \e
  \-\-html /var/lib/cti\-agent/state/domains\-$(date \-u +%F).html \-\-dry\-run
.EE
.PP
A one-off send to someone outside the allowlist, after approval on the board:
.PP
.EX
sudo cti\-agent cti\-mailer \-\-html report.html \e
  \-\-to analyst@example.com \-\-require\-approval \-\-approve
.EE
.PP
Ask the operator a question:
.PP
.EX
sudo cti\-agent cti\-mailer \-\-to\-operator \-\-board\-id q17 \e
  \-\-subject "Approve off\-cycle send?" \-\-message "Draft is on the board."
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR run\-appscan (1),
.BR run\-domains (1),
.BR run\-digest (1),
.BR cti\-mailbox (1),
.BR cti\-alert (1),
.BR cti\-agent (1)
.PP
RUNBOOK.md section 11b, "Switching the mailer"; sections 11f and 11g for the
.B was
and
.B dom
lanes;
.IR fleet.env.example ,
section 4.
